<!--
  Declared breaks against 1.0.0-beta.1, permitted by the repository's prerelease-stability policy and
  required by it to be declared. The SQLite and PostgreSQL stores implement the scoped, guarded, paged
  Docket contract (dropping the two unscoped expiry members and the unscoped amendments overwrite),
  MarkBlockedAsync takes a scope like every other member that moves a row, and every store takes an
  injectable TimeProvider as an added constructor parameter so expiry can be read as state against a
  clock a test can move.

  See CHANGELOG.md's upgrade notes.
-->
